  "notes": "USAGE:\nVery common in product descriptions and daily life. Appears on rice cookers, thermoses, heated tables, and clothing labels. Often seen as a button or setting label on appliances.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {保温|ほおん}{機能|きのう} (heat-retention function)\n- {保温|ほおん}する (to keep warm)\n- {保温|ほおん}ボトル (insulated bottle)\n- {保温性|ほおんせい} (heat-retention properties)\n- {保温|ほおん}モード (keep-warm mode)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {保冷|ほれい}: keeping cool — the opposite; maintaining cold temperature\n- {断熱|だんねつ}: insulation — preventing heat transfer in either direction",
